+# ACP Post-Publication Release Audit
+
+## Purpose
+
+`CONFORMANCE/release_audit.py` verifies every stable ACP tag against the
+published Gitea release and its two-stage evidence. It is read-only: it never
+creates, edits, deletes, or republishes a tag, release, asset, or secret.
+
+The audit runs daily and can be started through `workflow_dispatch` immediately
+after the attestation asset is uploaded. It deliberately does not use the
+Gitea `release: published` event: the attestation is produced after the release
+exists, so that event can run before the required asset upload. Normal
+pull-request CI runs only the deterministic fixtures in
+`CONFORMANCE/test_release_audit.py`.
+
+## Verified Bindings
+
+For every tag matching `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, the audit requires:
+
+1. an annotated Git tag object;
+2. exactly one Gitea release for that tag;
+3. a non-draft, non-prerelease release with non-empty notes;
+4. `target_commitish` equal to the full peeled tag commit;
+5. exactly one `release-attestation.yaml` release asset;
+6. matching repository, version, tag-object ID, peeled commit and release URL;
+7. the SHA-256 of the published release notes;
+8. the exact set and SHA-256 hashes of all payload assets;
+9. pre-publication evidence present in the peeled target commit;
+10. an attestation timestamp after both tag creation and release publication;
+11. no `attestation_hash` and no attestation entry in its own `assets` list.
+
+Platform-generated source archives are not Gitea release assets and therefore
+are outside the explicit asset-set comparison.
+
+## Credential Contract
+
+The workflow reads the repository secret `ACP_RELEASE_AUDIT_TOKEN`. Gitea
+rejects secret names beginning with its reserved `GITEA_` prefix, so the name
+must not be changed to `GITEA_RELEASE_AUDIT_TOKEN`.
+
+Required scope:
+
+- `read:repository`
+
+Prohibited scopes:
+
+- all write scopes;
+- `write:user` or administrative scopes;
+- package, organization, issue, or release mutation permissions.
+
+Use a dedicated audit token owned by an identity with read access to
+`Homelab/ACP`. The token is stored only as a Gitea Actions repository secret.
+It must not be committed, included in review packages, passed as a command-line
+argument, or printed.
+
+## Operator Provisioning
+
+Credential creation and repository-secret mutation are explicit operator
+actions and are not performed by this implementation PR.
+
+1. Create a dedicated token with only `read:repository`.
+2. Add its raw value to the `Homelab/ACP` Actions repository secret named
+   `ACP_RELEASE_AUDIT_TOKEN`.
+3. Manually dispatch `ACP Post-Publication Release Audit` after provisioning
+   and after each stable release has its attestation asset.
+4. Confirm the `credential-preflight` and `post-publication-audit` steps pass.
+5. Rotate by replacing the secret value, then revoke the previous token.
+
+The workflow uses the LAN API endpoint configured in
+`.gitea/workflows/release-audit.yaml`; the endpoint is non-secret.
+
+## Local Deterministic Verification
+
+```bash
+python3 CONFORMANCE/test_release_audit.py
+```
+
+The local suite does not contact Gitea and uses no credential. The authenticated
+adapter can be invoked manually only when the read-only token is already in the
+environment:
+
+```bash
+export GITEA_API_URL=http://192.168.2.30:3000/api/v1
+# ACP_RELEASE_AUDIT_TOKEN must already exist in the process environment.
+python3 CONFORMANCE/release_audit.py --repository Homelab/ACP \
+  --token-env ACP_RELEASE_AUDIT_TOKEN --json
+```
+
+## Runtime Boundary
+
+This audit proves publication binding only. It does not prove that any runtime
+consumer is deployed, synchronized, or pinned to the release. Runtime-consumer
+state remains a separate release gate and evidence record.
